<.flash_group flash={@flash} />
<h1>Boardlist Configuration</h1>

<p><a href={~p"/manage"}>Back to dashboard</a></p>

<p :if={@error} class="error"><%= @error %></p>

<p>
  Configure boardlist groups separately for desktop and mobile. Each value must be a JSON array of groups using board URIs as strings or label-to-URL maps.
</p>
<p>
  Link labels support the same placeholders as the global message. Inline conditional text can use <code>{if tf2_display &gt; N}conditional text</code>; the text after the condition is hidden unless the player count is greater than the integer threshold <code>N</code>.
</p>
<br />
<p>See this example:</p>

<pre>
{
  "desktop": [
    ["a", "b", "c", "j", "qa"],
    {"rules": "/rules"},
    {"faq": "/faq", "format": "/formatting"},
    {"Booru": "https://gyate.net", "TF2 {if tf2_display > 0}TF2 playercount: {tf2_display}/24": "https://kogasa.tf"},
    {"Home": "/"}
  ],
  "mobile": [
    ["a", "b", "j"],
    {"rules": "/rules"},
    {"Home": "/"}
  ]
}</pre>
<form action={~p"/manage/boardlist/browser"} method="post">
  <input type="hidden" name="_csrf_token" value={get_csrf_token()} />
  <input type="hidden" name="_method" value="patch" /> <textarea
    name="boardlist_json"
    rows="18"
    style="width:100%"
  ><%= @boardlist_json %></textarea>
  <p><input type="submit" value="Update boardlist" /></p>
</form>
